-- The Boss loot index, without its loot. docs/boss-loot.md in the pipeline is the contract. The addon joins it to BossLoot.lua, whose loot lists it names by creature (c) and chest object (ob) id, into the table the contract describes.
-- { v = 1, s = {strings}, p = {places, in draw order}, b = {bosses, rares and chests}, it = { [itemId] = type * 1000 + item level } }. v is the contract version; refuse any other.
-- p = { n name (index into s), k kind (1 dungeon, 2 raid, 3 world boss), lv the level the band is read from (1 to 60), lo/hi the level range, m Map id, a the area id EraSources uses, an the AreaTable name where it differs from n, z (k=3) the zones (pfQuest's, then those of its EraSources pins and paths), po (k=3) 1 = its places are shared, it stands at one of them at a time, ez the entrance zone's name (absent for k=3), ec the continent's name, eu/ex/ey the entrance pin (the zone UiMapID, and x from the left and y from the top in tenths of a percent, 0 to 1000; all three or none; the instance portal), mu/mx/my the outdoor mouth players look for, where it is hand checked (the same shape as eu/ex/ey; all three or none; either set may be there without the other), sz players, g 1 = new in Forever, b = {indices into b, in draw order} }. Places are in draw order: band (ceil(lv / 10), 1 to 6; 7 endgame, lv 60 or k=3; 8 no lv), then lv, then k, then name.
-- b = { n name, r rank (1 boss, 2 rare elite, 3 rare, 4 chest), lo/hi creature levels, e the EraSources s index of the name, ei the creature id its Classic Era page is keyed by (EraSources' ci of e: the page is npc: .. -ei, or npc: .. ei where em is 1), em 1 = that page is one page with the Forever creature's (EraPlaces' cm), cd the CreatureDisplayInfo id of the first creature in c this build has a model for, ct its CreatureType, c creature ids, ob (r=4) the chest's object ids, d DungeonEncounter id, g 1 = an encounter new in Forever with no CMaNGOS creature, w world drops left out, cl the community drops of its creatures (the l record shape, value always 0: no chance ships; Predicted until the player's own records replace them) }. Every key but n and r is optional. Bosses first (encounter order), then rares by level and name, then chests by name.
-- it: every item an entry's loot names, as its type code times 1000 plus its item level (0 = unknown), from this build's own item tables. The join makes each entry's l (the contract's fixed 8 byte records: item id (3), value (2), type (1), item level (2)) out of BossLoot.lua's records of its creatures or objects, each item at its best drop, an item it does not hold left out, in draw order: type, then chance descending with none last, then item level descending, then id.
-- Types: 1 Plate, 2 Mail, 3 Leather, 4 Cloth, 5 Back, 6 Shield, 7 Held in off-hand, 8 Neck, 9 Finger, 10 Trinket, 11 Relic, 12 One-hand weapon, 13 Two-hand weapon, 14 Ranged, 15 Recipe, 16 Quest, 17 Material, 18 Consumable, 19 Container, 20 Key, 21 Other.
